            "body": "<!-- pr-pundit-live:primus-1368-d41e908d -->\n### PR Pundit review\n1 finding.\n\n| # | | Finding | Where |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 🔵 | Next regeneration flips provenance comments back, causing noisy diffs: this PR regenerated from a different directory | `docs/sphinx/requirements.txt:193` |\n\n<details><summary>Nits and less certain findings (1)</summary>\n\n**1. Next regeneration flips provenance comments back, causing noisy diffs: this PR regenerated from a different directory** (`docs/sphinx/requirements.txt:193`)\n\nThe regeneration changed the `# via -r docs/sphinx/requirements.in` annotations (lines 193, 246) to `# via -r requirements.in`. The header still documents `pip-compile docs/sphinx/requirements.in` run from the repo root, so the next regeneration will flip them back and create noisy diffs. Restore the original annotations, or align the header with how the file is actually compiled.\n\n**Who is affected:** Maintainers who regenerate or review the docs lockfile; documentation builds are unaffected.\n\n_Checked against the code by an independent pass._\n\n</details>",
